From 5c3bb41c51e4081aae82f112872aae8a5432aa2d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <stew675@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 15:15:53 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] gap-closing WIP: MMB quant coverage -- Q4_0, Q4_1, Q5_0,
 MXFP4, NVFP4

Add five more GGUF weight types to the MMB (dequant->bf16 WMMA) path: new
WTYPE codes 11=Q4_0, 12=Q4_1, 13=Q5_0, 14=MXFP4, 15=NVFP4, with exact-size byte
dequantizers (mmb_dq_row_q4_0/_q4_1/_q5_0/_mxfp4/_nvfp4) wired through the
dense, routed (MUL_MAT_ID) and fused gate+up+GLU launches + the type masks.

Validated on gfx1151:
- test-backend-ops MUL_MAT with MMB forced on (GGML_CUDA_MMB_MIN_T=1):
  q4_0 48/48, q4_1 47/47, q5_0 14/14, mxfp4 46/46, nvfp4 45/45.
- test-backend-ops MUL_MAT_ID: q4_0 74/74, q4_1 75/75, q5_0 3/3, mxfp4 74/74,
  nvfp4 73/73.
- PPL (16 chunks) off->on: Q4_0 27.59->27.54, Q4_1 25.74->25.16, Q5_0
  22.02->21.69; gpt-oss-20b MXFP4 (8 chunks) 677.0->670.4.
- pp throughput off->on: Nanbeige-3B pp8192 Q4_0 +19.5 %, Q4_1 +22.4 %,
  Q5_0 +25.4 %; 35B-A3B Q4_1 pp4096 1500 -> 2449 (+63 %, routed+GLU);
  gpt-oss-20b MXFP4 pp4096 2156 -> 2267 (+5.2 %).
- existing types unregressed (iq4_nl 14/14, q8_0 50/50).

Default-enable the new types on non-RDNA4 (the Q4Q5 mask arm); RDNA4 keeps its
per-type dense policy, so they stay inert there.  NVFP4 has no local model, so
its throughput is unmeasured -- the MUL_MAT/MUL_MAT_ID oracles are its gate.
